load @term/seed/structure/set
  find set

# A topological space: a set together with a choice of which subsets count as open, closed under arbitrary unions and
# finite intersections, with the empty set and the whole set open. The open sets are what "near" means without any
# notion of distance, the minimum needed to speak of continuity, limits, and connectedness. Every metric space is a
# topological space, but topology keeps only the qualitative shape. The mesh, the hyperbolic honeycomb of the substrate,
# is a topological space whose growth is one-way. The form carries the underlying set; the family of open sets and its
# closure laws are the axioms.
form topological-space
  link set, like set
